    <string name="advanced_focus_accessibility_description">Pomodoro uses the AccessibilityService API only while you have Focus Mode turned on. It detects which app comes to the foreground so it can pause the apps you chose to block during a focus session, and in Strict lock it also detects navigation keys (Back, Home, Recents and the notification shade) so you stay inside Pomodoro. It never reads screen content, never records what you type, and never collects, stores or shares personal data. Your blocked-app list stays on this device.</string>
